Fix a crash when inferring a comparison that tests membership of an
out-of-range byte value, such as ``257 in b""``. ``_do_compare`` only caught
``TypeError``, letting ``ValueError: byte must be in range(0, 256)`` escape
and crash the caller (e.g. pylint's ``safe_infer``). ``ValueError`` is now
caught alongside ``TypeError``, so the comparison is uninferable instead,
consistent with the existing ``123 <= "abc"`` path.

Closes #3333
